Ideas for new boots:

Boots of Stepguarding
When worn, they prevent the player from stepping on ground that would
cause him harm.  They work by preventing movement, not making the
player safe, and they waste a turn in the process.  They prevent the
player from stepping, specifically, from ground traps, intrinsically
harmful objects, or dangerous features there.  Thus, they would make
it so the player could not step on water or lava tiles, or traps that
are considered to be mechanical in nature, known or not, unless the
boots are removed.  This means: pit traps, spiked pits, trap doors,
holes, rolling boulder traps, land mines, beartraps, sleep traps,
arrow traps and dart traps. They do not identify or reveal a trap,
just prevent movement.  Trap types that are magical in nature, like
polymorph, teleport, level teleport, magic traps, anti-magic traps and
portals, will not be guarded against.  Fire and rust are uncertain
cases, but I'm of the opinion that, if it's not obviously a trap
<i>that is stepped on</i>, then it shouldn't count.  These boots would
work on undiscovered terrain tiles and traps, so they could be very
useful to a low-level character worried about pit traps.

As a consequence of their function, they would also prevent stepping
on a cockatrice corpse, because of the danger while blind, and they
would even function to prevent movement onto dangerous squares due to
confusion, stunning, blindness or hallucination.  These boots do not
take the player's state into account, so a sighted player, or one
wearing gloves, and wearing these boots would still not be able to
walk on cockatrice corpse.

Boots of Running
Decreases energy required to move, but provides no extra attacks.
That is to say, a player could more readily run from a monster, or
walk around it, but should he fight he is effectively slowed to his
real speed.  Should not make the player faster than someone who
continually jumps with jumping boots, but should make his run speed
faster than speed boots.  Since the only permanent way to increase
speed to Very Fast is with speed boots, the player must effectively
choose between faster movement or extra actions (or jumping).

Boots of Wandering
Causes the player to move randomly instead of the desired direction
about once every ten moves on average.  Usually generated cursed.  If
the move would take the player into a wall, he simply rests that turn
instead.  Moves into water or lava are punished as usual, as are
attacks against peacefuls or friendlies.  As a small compensation,
they protect against the more-frequent random movement part of
confusion and stunning (explained because its own random movement
would conflict with that caused by the confusion -- if it doesn't make
sense to you, well, it's magic).

